# Ship last week's logs

List the log directory "/var/log/app" as Logs.

For each file in Logs:
- If it is older than 7 days:
  - Compress the log file, then upload it to the backup url "s3://acme-backups/logs", then delete the log file.
    If it fails, connect to "https://hooks.example.com/oncall" (nothing is removed unless its archive arrived).

This section only reads from the log directory "/var/log/app" and only deletes from "/var/log/app" and only connects to "s3://acme-backups" and "https://hooks.example.com" and never runs.

# Back up the config

Read the config file "/etc/app/config.json" as Settings.
Write Settings to the backup file "/backup/config.json".
If it fails, delete the backup file "/backup/config.json" because a truncated backup misleads whoever restores it.

This section never deletes from "/etc" and only writes to the backup directory "/backup" and always reads from "/etc/app".

# Clear stale scratch space

List the temporary directory "/var/tmp/app" as Leftovers.

For each file in Leftovers:
- If the temporary file is older than 3 days or it is larger than 2 GB, delete it.

This section only deletes from "/var/tmp/app" and never connects.

# Publish the status page

Fetch the url "https://status.example.com/index.html" as Page.
Upload the public Page to "https://cdn.example.com/status/index.html".

This section only connects to "https://status.example.com" and "https://cdn.example.com" and uploads at most 1 times.
